## Step 1: set the project default location to `me-central2`

Google's docs list three policies: same region as the source disk (local-region), nearest multi-region, or a specific location, where only one location can be given.

| Option | Behavior | Fit |
|---|---|---|
| `local-region` | Follows each disk's region, so `me-central2` for all your disks | Flexible, but a disk created elsewhere would put snapshots elsewhere |
| `specific-locations` = `me-central2` | Always `me-central2` | Explicit, and easier to show an auditor |

I recommend `specific-locations`:
```bash
gcloud compute snapshot-settings update --storage-location-policy=specific-locations --storage-location-names=me-central2
```
I found only this command in the docs, not a Console path, so I'm giving you the command. It's a one-line change that you can reverse by running it again with the old policy.

