## What each step affects

| Step | Affects | Downtime | Cost | Reversible |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1. Project default | Only new snapshots, project-wide (anyone creating snapshots in this project) | none | none | yes, run the command with the old policy |
| 2. Delete 8 snapshots | Only those backups. The running servers and `clean-ubuntu-26092026-img` are unaffected, because the image was made from the disk, not from these snapshots | none | saves storage | no |
| 3. New schedule | The disks you attach it to | none | small recurring storage | yes, detach and delete |

**Trade-off:** a single region means a regional outage can't be recovered from snapshots. Your rule requires it, so it's accepted, but tell whoever owns DR.

**Encryption in transit:** nothing to configure. Google encrypts that traffic by default, so the fix is evidence, not a setting.

